              "aT": "Financing BESS in Italy: a balancing act between risk and expected returns",
              "aD": "BESS can be financed in Italy, but lenders need clarity on performance, control, contracts, and downside scenarios. This session unpacks the credit committee logic behind bankable storage and shows how to package a BESS project to shorten time-to-term sheet\n•\tPresent an engineering and degradation case that survives independent engineer scrutiny\n•\tStructure availability guarantees, warranties, and liquidated damages to support leverage\n•\tBuild covenant packages (DSCR, reserves, cash sweeps) that match merchant/tolling risk profiles\n•\tAllocate dispatch rights, operating responsibilities, and compliance obligations in bankable terms\n•\tPrepare a lender-ready data pack that reduces diligence loops and accelerates closing\n",
