              "aT": "Regulatory & and auction risk: pricing uncertainty into deals without killing them",
              "aD": "Italy’s market remains investable, but regulatory risk is no longer theoretical. From auction design to potential retroactive cuts to Conto Energia tariffs, changes to interconnection requirements and “aree idonee” constraints to proposals affecting legacy incentives, this session focuses on how sophisticated investors and lenders price risk, and how developers can structure around it.\n•\tAnticipate auction eligibility and timing impacts on pipeline strategy and financing windows\n•\tUnderwrite retroactive-risk scenarios for legacy incentive assets and reflect them in valuation and covenants\n•\tNavigate “aree idonee” and permitting constraints within a financeable development roadmap\n•\tEmbed contractual protections (longstops, termination rights, conditions precedent) to manage policy risk\n•\tProtect downside by aligning permitting/interconnection status with milestone-based capital deployment\n",
